346. Calendar 🔴

Suppose a date picker requires selecting:

September 20, 2026

A common approach is to navigate month/year and select the day.

Basic example
driver.findElement(By.id("datePicker")).click();

while (true) {

    String month = driver.findElement(
            By.cssSelector(".calendar-month")
    ).getText();

    if (month.equals("September 2026")) {
        break;
    }

    driver.findElement(
            By.xpath("//button[@aria-label='Next month']")
    ).click();
}

driver.findElement(
        By.xpath("//button[normalize-space()='20']")
).click();
Interview explanation

"For a dynamic calendar, I first compare the displayed month and year with the target month and year. If they don't match, I navigate using the next or previous month button and finally select the required day."

Important

Don't blindly locate:

//button[text()='20']

because multiple 20 elements may exist from previous/next month.

