358. Broken links 🔴🔴

This is a very common coding interview question.

List<WebElement> links =
        driver.findElements(By.tagName("a"));

for (WebElement link : links) {

    String url = link.getAttribute("href");

    if (url == null || url.isBlank()) {
        continue;
    }

    HttpURLConnection connection =
            (HttpURLConnection)
                    new URL(url).openConnection();

    connection.setRequestMethod("HEAD");

    connection.connect();

    int statusCode =
            connection.getResponseCode();

    if (statusCode >= 400) {

        System.out.println(
                "Broken: " + url +
                " --> " + statusCode
        );

    } else {

        System.out.println(
                "Valid: " + url +
                " --> " + statusCode
        );
    }
}
Interview explanation

"I collect all anchor elements, extract their href values, send an HTTP request to each URL and validate the response status code. Generally, 400 and above indicate an unsuccessful response, though the exact handling can depend on the application."

