361. Pagination 🔴🔴

Suppose every page contains a table.

while (true) {

    List<WebElement> rows =
            driver.findElements(
                    By.xpath("//table[@id='data']//tbody/tr")
            );

    for (WebElement row : rows) {
        System.out.println(row.getText());
    }

    WebElement next =
            driver.findElement(
                    By.xpath("//button[@aria-label='Next']")
            );

    if (!next.isEnabled()) {
        break;
    }

    next.click();

    new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10))
            .until(ExpectedConditions.stalenessOf(rows.get(0)));
}
Interview concept

You should explain:

Read current page
      ↓
Process rows
      ↓
Check Next button
      ↓
If enabled → click
      ↓
Wait for next page
      ↓
Repeat
      ↓
Stop when Next disabled
